low). Read TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev11.md, the review logbook and materialize TASK-260909-2ez769_review-evidence-rev11.zip (callsite_probe.py, reviewer_callsite_test.go, callsite-plant.txt, callsite.log; reviewer_binding_test.go with rebind-final.log). Base is the checkpoint 305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d on trunk 8626fb36 (first git fetch origin; if origin/main moved, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260909-2ez769 and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>); CR11 candidate tree 11a860063bb9802361f7d1883dff8ad64681ba94 in .temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree — continue from it. Preserve the checkpointed SSH/peer leaves, the parked RPC artifacts and the control-root backup with their recorded hashes; no RPC transport; no manual commits; no direct .task-board edits; no self-acceptance. Superseded briefs are scope context only; this brief governs.\n4|\n5|CR11 confirmed the ResolvedPaths-bound pair model (the old foreign-root attack is refused; 17/17 standalone census plants detected). Four items remain; fix exactly these:\n6|\n7|F1 (P2, call-site admission): writepath_census_types_test.go builds a set of interface method objects per enclosing function (around :490) and authorizes every call of that object anywhere inside that function (:681; method values at :775), so a conditional filesystem.Rename inserted at the beginning of replaceDurably BEFORE requireHoldForConfig is admitted (census PASS, witness renames a real file with a zero hold and zero pair, exit 0). Repair: an admitted indirect edge must be identified by (callee object, enclosing declaration object, exact call-site position) and must be dominated by the hold verification in the same function body — the gate checks that every admitted call site occurs after the requireHold*/hold-verification statement on every path (statement order within the function body and no path around it), and any new call or escaped meth