{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c58d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6d-f2e1-7d43-9e77-843c8eea6221"},"sequence":289,"recorded_at":1780531400000573,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"9d656e52-9607-486f-955f-021a4f63ae37","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"9d656e52-9607-486f-955f-021a4f63ae37","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"9d656e52-9607-486f-955f-021a4f63ae37"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6f-1b14-7160-a0fa-93c69642022c"},"task_id":"01a0ad6f-1b14-7160-a0fa-93c69642022c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ad6f-1b14-7160-a0fa-93c69642022c","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev11.md`.\n1|# CR11 review verdict: changes requested\n2|\n3|Task TASK-260909-2ez769, CR-TASK-260909-2ez769-11 revision 11.\n4|Reviewer RUN-260917-6165a9. Base 305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d;\n5|candidate tree 11a860063bb9802361f7d1883dff8ad64681ba94.\n6|Patch SHA-256 75bc1326120283632cf2afd0129598e84bc3be69d9d59e0e11dff310494ed9a0.\n7|All probes ran in an archive of this immutable tree under\n8|`.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/review11/candidate`. No live Story source, index,\n9|branch, HEAD, checkpoint or integration was changed.\n10|\n11|## F1 — P2: interface exceptions still authorize new call sites\n12|\n13|Repeat-of CR10 F1 / CR9 F1 / CR8 F1 / CR7 F1 / CR6 F3, narrowed to the\n14|explicit call-site requirement that CR11 still does not implement.\n15|The original Execute/name heuristic is repaired for standalone interface and\n16|type-parameter call boundaries. All 17 independent standalone plants are now\n17|killed by the census assertion, with all 17 actual-file runtime witnesses passing.\n18|This includes both CR10 direct Execute boundaries and two new shapes: a generic\n19|method value named Perform and a closure-returned function called through an\n20|interface. No compilation failure is counted as a kill.\n21|\n22|However `writepath_census_types_test.go:490` builds a set of method objects per\n23|enclosing function, and `:681` authorizes every call of that object anywhere\n24|inside that function. The policy does not identify a call site or enforce its\n25|position relative to the hold gate. `:775` similarly admits its method values.\n26|The source still contains a method-spelling predicate at `:783/:991`; that is\n27|not the counterexample here, but the report's blanket no-heuristic claim should\n28|be narrowed or the remaining admission path removed.\n29|\n30|Independent compiling plant: insert a conditional `filesystem.Rename` at the\n31|beginning of production `replaceDurably`, before `requireHoldForConfig`, using\n32|its existing filesystem interface. The planted branch is selected only by the\n33|reviewer witness. A zero hold and zero pair successfully rename a real file.\n34|`TestReviewerUnlistedSiteExecutes` PASS and `TestWritePathCensusGate` PASS;\n35|subprocess exit **0**. The original hold check and existing method-object tokens\n36|remain intact. This is a prevention-instrument counterexample, not a claim that\n37|the unmodified product currently contains that branch. See `callsite_probe.py`,\n38|`reviewer_callsite_test.go`, `callsite-plant.txt`, and `callsite.log`.\n39|\n40|Required repair: enumerate and check the exact required indirect edges AND\n41|call sites, with a production justification for each. A new call or escaped\n42|method value cannot inherit authorization solely from being inside a writer\n43|that already uses that interface method. Add this executable regression and a\n44|narrowing mutant that preserves method identity while broadening call-site\n45|admission. Do not merely add this one sentinel to the detector.\n46|\n47|## F2 — P2: a refused rebind durably claims a second configuration\n48|\n49|New failure introduced by the CR11 bidirectional binding repair; related to,\n50|but not a survival of, CR10 F2's foreign-store write.\n51|`hosttrust.ensureConfigBindingLocked` publishes the authoritative target record\n52|at `binding.go:254` before checking the existing store-side association at\n53|`:263–269`. A legitimate sequence using only production APIs is:\n54|\n55|1. Resolve (config A, state S) and (config B, state S).\n56|2. Open both Stores while S is unbound.\n57|3. Store A successfully calls EnsureConfigBinding(A,S).\n58|4. Already-open Store B calls EnsureConfigBinding(B,S).\n59|\n60|Step 4 returns ErrExclusiveHoldResourceMismatch, but only after it has durably\n61|written B's target sidecar naming S. The store-side index still names A. A later\n62|legitimate attempt to associate B with a different state root is now refused.\n63|The immutable one-store/one-config association is left contradictory by a\n64|refused request, with no crash or sidecar forgery involved.\n65|\n66|`TestReviewerRefusedRebindLeavesTargetUnclaimed` fails, actual exit **1**, after\n67|observing the persistent B sidecar and the subsequent legitimate-bind refusal.\n68|See `reviewer_binding_test.go`, `rebind-final.log`, and `rebind-final.exit`.\n69|Required repair: validate the existing store association under its exclusive\n70|lock before publishing any target association. Cover two handles opened before\n71|binding, sequential and competing binding requests, and failed requests leaving\n72|both existing and previously unclaimed target associations intact. Retain the\n73|explicit crash-repair path for a genuinely interrupted first binding.\n74|\n75|The old F2 counterexample IS repaired: a second genuine resolver-issued pair\n76|(target A, foreign state F) cannot bind A once A's authoritative target record\n77|names S, even while S's lock is held. `TestReviewerSecondResolvedPairRefused`\n78|and committed HeldExclusive controls pass, exit 0. ResolvedPaths has private\n79|fields; its getters return copies, and no constructor other than ResolvePaths\n80|mints its populated map. Public pair APIs now consume this value, or production\n81|Inputs/Overrides resolved through config.Load; pair writers consume the value.\n82|Root-string helpers remain for trust-file plumbing behind requireHoldForRoot;\n83|this is not falsely reported as 'no string path arguments anywhere'.\n84|\n85|## Evidence and repository hygiene\n86|\n87|The named board resource `TASK-260909-2ez769_producer-evidence-rev11.tar.gz` is\n88|ASCII prose, not an archive. `TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev11.md` is absent as a\n89|board resource (get returned resource-not-found). The local archive DOES exist,\n90|and SHA-256 b33b18fa31ce0df7db66f937b9c7f83cf0980f92d28f0b0e8bbd7c82b142d1ce\n91|matches the pointer; its outcome and raw logs were available for this review.\n92|Correct the attachment with resource update using the actual binary and attach\n93|the outcome independently before the next handoff. Local survival must not be\n94|mistaken for a portable evidence attachment.\n95|\n96|Remove the candidate's generated `internal/hosttrust/__pycache__/mutations.cpython-314.pyc`.\n97|x/tools is test-only; offline tidy and all three platform builds pass. README's\n98|tool row still describes writer-shaped calls, not the new all-indirect-call\n99|policy and its exact exceptions. Update it after F1 is fixed.\n100|\n101|## Functional AC accounting and limits\n102|\n103|**19 of 21 functional AC rows driven**, with rows 15 and 21 retained as stated\n104|bounds. This is the established functional decomposition, not exhaustive\n105|normative-clause coverage or discharge of F1/F2. Rechecked pinned v0.6.0 sections\n106|6.6, 11.10.2 and 11.10.3 against the local hash-verified source. All 43 exact test\n107|names in the table below resolve in the immutable candidate; generic suite\n108|labels additionally refer to the package runs. The new binding failure is not\n109|hidden by this functional ratio.\n110|\n111|| # | Acceptance row | Production call / named test evidence | Result |\n112||---:|---|---|---|\n113|| 1 | Closed Config4 | `config.Decode`; `TestDecodeConfiguration4Refusals` | pass |\n114|| 2 | Historical compatibility + explicit migration | `config.Migrate`/legacy migration; `TestMigrateRefusesV4Target`, `TestMigrateRefusesV4Downgrade`, `TestLegacyMigrateCannotOverwriteCommittedV4`, `TestLegacyMigrateConvergesUnreplacedMarkerThenCommits`, `TestLegacyMigrateRefusesAfterReplacementLanded` | pass |\n115|| 3 | Closed trust document | `hosttrust.DecodeTrust`; `TestDecodeTrustRefusals` | pass |\n116|| 4 | Missing/corrupt/unreadable trust | `hosttrust.ReadSnapshot`; `TestReadSnapshotMissingStore`, `TestCorruptTrustRefusedNeverEmpty`, `TestReadSnapshotRefusesUnreadableMarker` | pass |\n117|| 5 | Fresh issuance | `hosttrust.IssueCredential`; `TestIssueCredentialProfile`, `TestIssueSelfEnrollsActive` | pass |\n118|| 6 | Exact profile + time bounds | `hosttrust.VerifyProfile`; `TestVerifyProfileRefusals`, `TestVerifyProfileRefusesJustPastExpiry`, wrong-key-usage/EKU/SAN tests | pass |\n119|| 7 | Explicit tuple enrollment | `hosttrust.Store.Enroll`; `TestEnrollRefusals`, `TestEnrollBoundsPerHost`; OOB human verification remains an operator act | pass within stated OOB boundary |\n120|| 8 | Mapping uniqueness | `hosttrust.DecodeTrust` + admission; duplicate credential/root/key/digest cases in `TestDecodeTrustRefusals`, `TestEnrollBoundsPerHost`, and lifecycle tests | pass |\n121|| 9 | Rotation/retirement bounds | `hosttrust.Rotate`, `MarkRetiring`; `TestRotateBoundedWindow`, `TestRotateCapsAtLeafExpiry`, `TestMarkRetiringCapsAtLeafExpiry` | pass |\n122|| 10 | Revocation tombstones | `hosttrust.Revoke`, `Enroll`; `TestRevokeTombstone`, `TestRevokedLeafNeverReenrolls`, `TestRevocationClosesAuthorization` | pass |\n123|| 11 | Old-generation mutation refusal | `hosttrust.WithMutationAuthorization`; `TestWithMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleGeneration`, `TestMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleAfterConvergence` | pass |\n124|| 12 | Shared authorization serialization | `hosttrust.Open`/lock, `WithMutationAuthorization`, `Revoke`; `TestFirstOpenPreservesHeldLock`, `TestConcurrentOpenAttachesToExistingLock`, `TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithRevocation`, `TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithSeparateStoreRevocation` | pass |\n125|| 13 | Coherent config+trust snapshot | `config.LoadCoherent`; `TestSurvivingReaderConvergesInterruptedApply`, `TestSurvivingReaderConvergesInterruptedRollback`, `TestSurvivingReaderRefusesDivergedConfig`, barrier and revalidation tests | pass |\n126|| 14 | Unix owner custody | `hosttrust.Open`, `ValidateCustody`; `TestCustodyRefusals`, `TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory`, `TestOpenCreatesOwnerOnlyLayout` | pass on Darwin |\n127|| 15 | Windows equivalent ACLs | `verifyOwner`, `installOwnerOnlyACL`, `secureStaged`; `custody_windows_test.go` seven native tests | stated bound: no Windows runtime runner; cross-build, test-compile, and vet pass |\n128|| 16 | Complete peers + selected credential | `config.PreviewV4`; `TestPreviewV4PeerEnrollment`, `TestPreviewV4CredentialGates` | pass |\n129|| 17 | Exact preview + confirmation | `config.ApplyV4`; `TestApplyV4PreviewMismatch`, `TestApplyV4ConfirmRequiredWithDrops` | pass |\n130|| 18 | Current source/generation apply | Config4 apply + `hosttrust.JointCommit`; `TestApplyV4StaleSource`, `TestApplyV4StaleGeneration`, revalidation and stale-marker tests | pass |\n131|| 19 | Crash-durable config/trust pair | Config4 apply/rollback + `hosttrust.JointCommit`, `Recover`, convergence; `TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration`, surviving-reader/barrier/compensation tests | pass |\n132|| 20 | Explicit backup rollback | `config.RollbackV4`; `TestRollbackV4*`, `TestPublishedBackupNamesStayExcluded`, `TestApplyV4BackupIsClassifiedConfigCopy` | pass |\n133|| 21 | Secret exclusion across export surfaces | `hosttrust.MatchExcludedFromReplication`, `ExcludedConfigDirName`; matcher and persisted handoff/owner-note evidence | stated boun