78.0/config 93.5/peeridentity 97.5/secprim 94.4, 343 top-level PASS 0 FAIL across touched packages, fuzz 13/13, tracecheck/catalog/cigate/JSON/diff-check clean, task-board validate exit 0 with 0 issues for this task. 7 original + 2 F2 exact probes pass on final source. 19/21 AC rows driven, all passing; rows 15/21 retained bounded per CR5/CR6.\n44|+- LESSON: intermittent \"package X is not in std\"/\"could not import\" battery failures were external go-build-cache interference (different plants each run; serial re-runs kill); batteries re-run with a private GOCACHE. Never run concurrent `go` commands during overlay batteries on this machine.\n45|+\n46|+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev6 — CR5 unlocked-compensation finding repaired as a class\n47|+- F1: `JointCommit` takes the restore closure and compensates a failed bump under the SAME exclusive hold (`compensateLocked`): marker re-read pin-for-pin, config hash must equal the replacement pin, restore result verified against the source pin before the abort. No reader/writer/boundary can converge between failure and restore. The unlocked `restoreSourceAfterJointFailure` is deleted. Original CR5 probe RED (exit 1, quoted failure) pre-fix; post-fix its in-seam convergence blocks in `flock` (timeout dump proves the hold) and the ported `TestApplyV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit` pins the race as goroutine-vs-gated-restore.\n48|+- CENSUS: 12-row write-path census (`TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md` board outcome) covers every pair mutation incl. legacy `migrate` (fail-closed row, pinned by `TestLegacyMigrateBesideMarkerRefusesConvergence`), inert credential staging, atomic lock creation, and the sabotage remainder (vanished-marker re-stage). Enforced by committed static gate `TestWritePathCensusGate` + control `TestWritePathGateFlagsUnlockedCaller`; preserve-token order-swap plant `compensate-verify-before-restore` passes the gate and fails only behaviorally.\n49|+- INTERLEAVINGS: 6 deterministic gated-restore race tests (apply/rollback × reader/writer/held-boundary) + 2 production-entry clean-abort tests + 8 hosttrust compensation tests (tamper/corrupt/unreadable marker, noop+wrong-bytes restore verification, fail-after-write, source-present skip). TEST BUG FOUND BY RACE SUITE ITSELF: boundary tests deadlocked reading trust post-seam on the main goroutine — request now binds pre-seam with a comment.\n50|+- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 29 narrowing (incl. 4 compensate-*) + 1 call-site + neutral passed; config 6 semantic + 1 label + neutral passed; all plants pre-verified count==1 with exits from subprocess return codes. Full local CI replicated green (26 ok, 0 FAIL, 1 pre-existing SKIP; race 26 ok; cover hosttrust 77.9/config 93.3; tracecheck/catalog-6/cigate-contracts-6/claims-6/targets-2/fuzz-13/fixtures 51+59 zero-skip/windows-compile). 7 original reviewer probes re-pass; rows 15/21 retained bounded per CR5.\n51|+- BOUNDS RESTATED: verifyLockFile 500ms retry rechecks custody without pinning an inode (no external-replacement claim); power-loss beyond fsync unproven; Windows runtime unverified; diagnostics export unowned; spurious-bump corner aborts fail-safe.\n52|+\n53|+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev5 — CR4 surviving-reader + lock-init findings repaired\n54|+- F1: pending joint-commit marker is now a general admission barrier (`convergeLocked` + shared-to-exclusive dance `lockForConvergedRead`): every read/admission/transaction entry point converges or refuses before exposing a snapshot. Surviving stores converge exactly like reopened ones; stale bindings compare against the recovered generation (never refreshed). Real child-process crash tests (exit 77) cover surviving + reopened × apply + rollback, marker cleanup, and intervened refusal with marker kept.\n55|+- F2: lock init is atomic non-replacing (O_CREAT|O_EXCL / CREATE_NEW via `FileSystem.CreateExclusive`); losers open the existing inode. Existing-file verify retries 500ms for the create-to-secure window; non-regular refuses immediately. Deterministic cross-process first-open test pins returnedWhileHeld=false + sameInode=true; the replacing-rename mutant restores the exact reviewer failure shape.\n56|+- F3: native Windows custody tests written (7, build-tagged; vet + test-compile pass, runtime unverified); config backups classified (byte-exact config copies, 0600, excluded names; Windows backup DACLs a stated bound); row-21 handoff persisted with per-surface API/test obligations + notes on all 7 owned tasks, diagnostics explicitly unowned.\n57|+- MUTANT LESSON: a JointCommit converge-ignore mutant survives because the staged-marker refusal backstops it — error-ignoring mutants are unobservable where a file-level backstop stands. Paired instead: joint-converge-skip (call-site, killed) + recover-forward-no-bump (narrowing, kills 8 named convergence tests).\n58|+- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 25 narrowing + 1 call-site killed + neutral passed; config 4 semantic + 1 label + neutral passed; full local CI replicated green (test/race/cover/tracecheck/catalog/cigate/fuzz-13/fixtures/claims/windows-compile). 19 of 21 AC rows driven; rows 15 (Windows runtime) and 21 (consumers) bounded, not passed.\n59|+\n60|+## 2026-09-10 (refresh)\n61|+\n62|+### TASK-260909-2ez769 refresh — story base moved c1eff01 to a89328c (trunk 8cf4aaa + v0.6.0 adoption)\n63|+- REFRESH: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` with exclusive lease (RUN-260910-a4ac2c). Round 1 (43c0e2b peer-identity): 5 file resolutions — LOGBOOK merged newest-first, README trunk + peer tail, 3 traceability files trunk-wins (v0.6.0 registry pin authoritative; v0.5.0 digest superseded). Round 2 (c1eff01 SSH): 4 resolutions reusing round-1 bytes + README with SSH `## SSH stdio transport` section appended and peer-section wording. Packet schema learned from tool errors: entries {checkpoint_oid, path, sha256, content-base64}. Both replayed commits signed oparin@me.com (41106b6, a89328c, verify-commit Good).\n64|+- COMBI