ate` still refuses (\"requires the final unresolved leaf\"). No vendoring, no manual rebase. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED for snapshot.\n80|+\n81|+## 2026-09-10\n82|+\n83|+### TASK-260909-2ez769 — Host Trust Store 1.0.0 + Config 4.0.0 migration implemented\n84|+- SCOPE: new `internal/hosttrust` (trust reader/writer, Profile-1 issuance/verify, custody, enroll/rotate/MarkRetiring/revoke, generation authz, export/exclusion); Config 4.0.0 reader/validator/encoder + Preview/Apply/Rollback in `internal/config`; v4 peeridentity interop test; secprim census extended to hosttrust.\n85|+- FINDING: peer rotation catch-up had no local path (only self-rotation). Added `Store.MarkRetiring` with the same 24h/enrolled_at bounds. `ensureOwnerDir` verifies existing dirs, never repairs: silent narrowing masked a widened dir (caught by TestCustodyRefusals).\n86|+- FINDING: Go x509 puts the CN ATV into Subject.Names (len 1), so CN-only means exactly one CN-OID ATV, not empty Names. Parsed-name check fixed in `profile_checks.go:subjectIsOnlyCN`.\n87|+- FINDING: encoding/json decodes `\"1\"` into json.Number; generation now requires a bare JSON number. Duplicate JSON keys audited via token stream before decode.\n88|+- DECISION: base refresh refused by tooling (\"candidate refresh requires the final unresolved leaf\"); no manual rebase. Candidate sits on c1eff01 citing v0.6.0 by value; adoption files not duplicated. Integration must land onto the adoption base.\n89|+- VALIDATION: 21/21 AC rows driven; 11 hosttrust + 3 config narrowing mutants killed (named), 1 label-precision kill, 2 neutral controls; `go test ./...` all ok; config refusal-inventory + secprim census green.\n90|+- STATUS: ready for review, worktree UNCOMMITTED for handoff snapshot.\n91|+\n92| ## 2026-09-09\n93| \n94| ### TASK-260908-2tkufa: recovered v0.6.0 consumer adoption and bound pending runtime owners\n95|@@ -1227,3 +1310,33 @@ assertion here rather than a brittle one.\n96| - EVIDENCE: 15-row battery, 6 behavioural kill