ing coverage via `revoke-state` + serialization tests.\n106|+- P1 CRASH ATOMICITY: new joint commit (`joint.go`): closed `PendingCommit` marker, `JointCommit` (in-lock revalidation + marker + replace + bump + unmark), `Recover` (forward/abort/refuse) auto-run by `Open`. `CommitConfigChange` removed (it encoded the split-brain pattern). Apply/rollback revalidate preview/source/generation/custody inside the exclusive hold; post-bump failures restore source + converge via `Recover` (`ErrJointReplacementDurable`). Committed real child-process crash test (`TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration`, exit 77) plus abort/intervention/already-bumped/exhaustion unit tests. Power-loss vs process-crash documented honestly (fsync-durable, disk-dependent).\n107|+- P1 WINDOWS DACL: `verifyOwner` now audits owner SID plus every DACL allow entry (null/empty/deny-only/unknown-type fail closed); creation paths install protected owner-only DACLs (`secureStaged`); Unix mode checks abstracted via `platformModeOK` (exact 0700/0600 preserved). Pure `ownerOnlyGrants` evaluator tested on darwin (9 cases). No Windows runner exists here: evidence is GOOS=windows build + vet clean, unit tests, and an explicit stated bound (no invented runtime pass).\n108|+- P2 EXCLUSION: `ExcludedFromReplication` gains the joint marker; new `MatchExcludedFromReplication` (staging prefixes, fail-closed escapes) and `ExcludedConfigDirName` (.bak./.pre-rollback./.ax-config-*) with custody-walk + published-backup-name tests. No in-repo replication/snapshot/export-of-state surface exists (sessadapter/localstore/dirnode do not touch host-channel); outcome hands consumers + required tests to future export surfaces. Config claim corrected: 4 semantic narrowing + 1 label-precision kill (label plant marked LABEL-PRECISION in-table).\n109|+- ROW 13: new production `LoadCoherent` (config+trust under one shared hold) + serialization test.\n110|+- VALIDATION (rerun this run, exit 0): gofmt clean; `go vet ./...`; `go test ./... -count=1` all ok (281 top-level PASS across hosttrust/config/peeridentity/secprim); `-cover` hosttrust 77.8 config 93.1 peeridentity 97.5 secprim 94.4; `-race` on hosttrust+config ok; tracecheck ok; catalog v0.6.0 -check ok; linux+windows amd64 builds ok; `git diff --check` clean; refusal-inventory audit green (new sites covered by direct revalidation/helper tests); census green. Mutation batteries rerun exact-source: hosttrust 18 narrowing KILLED + neutral passed; config 4 semantic + 1 label KILLED + neutral passed (manifests bound to a89328c in mutations-*-rework/).\n111|+- STATUS: ready for review, worktree UNCOMMITTED for handoff snapshot. `task-board validate` shows 231 pre-existing board-wide ledger-mirror issues, none referencing this task.\n112|+\n113|+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev8 — CR7 resource binding and typed write-path census\n114|+- BASE: managed `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260909-2ez769` advanced the candidate to protected AX trunk `8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`, replaying the checkpointed SSH/peer leaves. The RPC backup manifest and parked RPC delta remain preserved; no RPC implementation path was absorbed. Candidate branch head is `305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d` and remains uncommitted.\n115|+- FIX (F2): `HeldExclusive` now carries the exact trust-store root/lock identity and an explicit configuration-path binding. `requireHoldForRoot` protects hosttrust mutations; `ValidateConfigPath` protects Config4/legacy pair writes; `JointCommit` binds the marker path before replace/restore callbacks; legacy migration uses `WithExclusiveHoldForConfig`. A genuine hold from a different Store refuses before staging while the target lock is live (`TestWriteTempReplaceRefusesForeignStoreHold`). Zero, released, same-store, and unbound live holds are all production-position negative tests.\n116|+- FIX (F1): the Config/Host Trust Store write-path gate now loads production packages with `golang.org/x/tools/go/packages` and resolves `go/types` objects by package path, receiver, and method identity. It covers direct OS mutations, backend/interface methods, aliases, function/method values, map/struct fields, package initializers/IIFEs, closures, interface implementations, generic helpers, and unresolved callees (fail closed). The five CR7 plants plus direct controls and new interface/generic shapes have executable behavioral witnesses.\n117|+- EVIDENCE: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (`.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/go-test-all-01.log`); `go test ./... -cover` exit 0 (`config 93.5%`, `hosttrust 77.5%`, `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/go-test-cover-01.log`); `go vet ./...`, native build, GOOS=windows build/vet, gofmt, and `git diff --check` all exit 0. Census run: `writepath-census-02.log`. Narrowing mutants: `hold-resource-skip` killed by `TestHeldExclusiveRejectsUnboundConfigPath`; `replace-require-skip` killed by zero-hold production tests; token-preserving `writepath-method-value-skip` killed by `TestWritePathGateFlagsExecutableRogues/backend_method_value`. Raw mutation JSON/table are under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-{hold-resource,config-hold,writepath}-*/`.\n118|+- COVERAGE RATIO: 19 of 21 previously enumerated production acceptance rows are driven by named entry-point tests; 2 remain stated bounds (Windows runtime DACL execution and a future export/replication consumer surface absent from this repository). No claim is made for those bounds.\n119|+- STATUS: ready for review; worktree intentionally UNCOMMITTED for Story handoff snapshot.\n120|+\n121|+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev9 — CR8 narrowing closures for typed write census and Store-owned Config binding\n122|+- BASE: unchanged from rev8: candidate checkpoint `305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d`, protected AX trunk `8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`. The 15-file RPC backup manifest, parked RPC delta, and checkpointed SSH/peer work remain preserved; no RPC implementation path was absorbed.\n123|+- FIX (F1): the production-source write-path census now resolves `go/types` function identities for bare identifiers and selectors, while rejecting writer-shaped indirect callees unless they are an exact censused definition in the current Go build context. The census rejects dot-imported function values, promoted embedded backend methods, package-level slice writer functions, function-typed struct fields and parameters, and dot-imported composite-literal function values. `isHoldEntryCall` uses exact package/receiver/method identity, so a same-named impostor method is not an entry gate.\n124|+- FIX (F2): `WithExclusiveHoldForConfig` is Store-owned. A generic or foreign Store cannot bind an arbitrary existing Config path; a configured Store can bind only its canonical paired path. Refusal occurs before staging/bytes mutation. The narrowing mutant drops the unconfigured-store refusal while retaining the other path checks and is killed by `TestWithExclusiveHoldForConfigRefusesUnconfiguredStorePath`.\n125|+- EVIDENCE: `writepath-method-value-skip` preserves the searched token while weakening the typed method-value gate and is killed by `TestWritePathGateFlagsExecutableRogues/backend_method_value`; controls have executable witnesses for all six CR8 shapes. Hosttrust `hold-resource-skip` is killed by the unconfigured foreign-resource test. Final artifacts are under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-{config,hosttrust}-rev9/`.\n126|+- COVERAGE RATIO: 19 of 21 enumerated production acceptance rows are driven by named production-entry tests. The two stated bounds remain: Windows runtime DACL execution is not available on this Darwin runner, and this repository has no export/replication consumer surface for host-trust secret exclusion. No claim is made for either bound.\n127|+- VALIDATION: grouped full suite `go test -count=1 -v` A/B/C/D all exit 0 across all 26 packages; grouped full coverage A/B/C/D all exit 0 (`config 93.5%`, `hosttrust 77.9%`, `peeridentity 97.5%`); scoped hosttrust/config/peeridentity tests, scoped vet, native/Linux-arm64/Windows-amd64 builds, Windows test compilation, `go mod tidy -diff`, and `git diff --check` are green. Logs and package inventory are in `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/`.\n128|+- STATUS: ready for review; worktree remains intentionally UNCOMMITTED for Story handoff snapshot.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
