ion regression (child exit 0 under the mutant; outer test exit 1).\n+- F2: `ensureConfigBindingLocked` validates the store-side association and target-side association before publishing either side. A rejected second handle cannot leave a target claim behind; two handles opened before first binding publish exactly one winner; an interrupted first binding repairs the missing store index on reopen. RED evidence is `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/rebind-red-rev12.log`; the fixed production tests are `TestReviewerRefusedRebindLeavesTargetUnclaimed`, `TestCompetingFirstBindingsPublishExactlyOneAssociation`, and `TestInterruptedFirstBindingIsRepairedAfterReopen`.\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: Config4 has 1 neutral control plus 13 narrowing/precision mutants, all killed with named failures; Host Trust Store has 1 neutral control plus 34 narrowing/precision mutants, all killed. The Config4 and Host Trust Store mutation runs were split into bounded groups and each harness returned exit 0; raw overlays/results/tables are under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-*-rev12-*`. Generated `__pycache__` bytecode was removed and all later Python runs used `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`.\n+- VALIDATION: `go test ./internal/config -count=1 -v` exit 0 (81.286s) and `go test ./internal/hosttrust -count=1 -v` exit 0 (19.961s), including the new negative/recovery tests. Full repository validation and board evidence are recorded in the rev12 outcome before handoff.\n+- PRESERVATION/SCOPE: base moved by managed refresh-candidate to trunk `62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e` (replayed checkpoints `efe119a`/`5e54874`); candidate remains UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree. RPC backup/parked delta and checkpointed SSH/peer work remain outside this leaf. AC coverage remains 19 of 21 production rows; native Windows runtime ACL and downstream export/diagnostic consumers are explicit bounds. No RPC behavior, main integration, or review acceptance is claimed.\n+\n+## 2026-09-17\n+\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev11 — opaque resolved pair and current negative evidence\n+- F2: all pair-bearing production boundaries now consume the opaque `localstore.ResolvedPaths` minted by the single `localstore.ResolvePaths` resolver. `hosttrust.Open`, binding/hold validation, `JointCommit`, `LoadCoherent`, Config4 preview/apply/rollback, legacy migration, and pair writers no longer accept caller-supplied config/state tuples. The target-side binding record is authoritative; reopening a store with a derived binding but a missing target record refuses closed. The foreign-store target-binding probe is narrowing and killed by `TestWriteTempReplaceRefusesForeignStoreWithTargetBinding`.\n+- F1: the write-path census now compares exact `*types.Func` interface-method objects and rejects unlisted interface/type-parameter calls, parenthesized callees, and method values; executable real-file witnesses cover the new shapes. The preserved-token `writepath-interface-name-heuristic` mutant runs the behavioral suite and is killed.\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: current Config4 battery has 1 neutral control plus 13 unique narrowing/precision mutants, all killed (exit 1 with named production failures; `config-association-root-skip` was rerun in `part4b` and counted once). Current Host Trust Store battery has 1 neutral control plus 34 unique narrowing/precision mutants, all killed. One first-pass `hold-state-root-skip` compile failure was a harness defect; the corrected mutant rerun killed `TestHeldExclusiveRejectsForeignConfigStateRoot`, and the failed instrument run is not counted.\n+- VALIDATION: fresh `internal/config`, `internal/localstore`, `internal/hosttrust` tests, `go test ./... -v`, `go test ./... -cover`, `go vet ./...`, native/cross `go build`, cross test compilation with `go test -exec /usr/bin/true ./... -run '^$'` for darwin/linux/windows, `go mod tidy -diff`, gofmt, and `git diff --check` pass. The ordinary cross `go test -run '^$'` execution lane is retained as an expected host-format limitation (bad CPU/exec format), not a code pass.\n+- PRESERVATION/HANDOFF: RPC backup 15/15 and parked delta 11/11 remain byte-identical; checkpointed SSH/peer work is untouched; no RPC path was absorbed. Candidate remains UNCOMMITTED at `HEAD=305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d` on protected `origin/main=8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`. AC coverage remains 19 of 21 production rows; Windows runtime ACL (row 15) and downstream export/diagnostic consumers (row 21) are explicit bounds. Ready for developer-to-reviewer handoff; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n+\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev10 — Config4 binding and typed write-path census closed\n+- BASE/PRESERVATION: candidate was verified on current protected AX trunk (`origin/main=8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`, worktree HEAD `305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d`). The 15-file RPC backup and 11-file parked RPC delta remain byte-identical; checkpointed SSH/peer work remains present and no RPC implementation path was absorbed. Candidate changes remain UNCOMMITTED for the managed Story handoff.\n+- F1: Config4 now has an immutable, owner-only `config-binding.json` sidecar. Binding is explicit through `EnsureConfigBinding`; `JointCommit`, `LoadCoherent`, and pair writers require the existing binding and reject a missing, malformed, unreadable, rebound, or foreign state-root binding. The config-side selected `StateRoot` is compared to the canonical Host Trust Store root; no non-normative Config4 field was added to the closed `mesh.host_channel` table. `OpenForConfig` and the implicit legacy fallback were removed.\n+- F2: the write-path census is typed and fail-closed: unresolved calls, non-`*types.Func` call targets, and unlisted object identities are rejected; only explicit receiver/method, function-field, parameter/local, package-initializer, and external helper allowlists are accepted. New controls cover type-parameter method values, channel callbacks, and immediate function literals. The token-preserving `writepath-method-value-skip` mutant executes the behavioral suite and is killed.\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: Config4 battery has 1 neutral control passed and 11 narrowing/precision mutants killed; Host Trust Store battery has 1 neutral control passed and 34 narrowing/precision mutants killed, with zero survivors. Results are archived under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-config-final/` and the `mutations-hosttrust-rev10-*` directories. Initial relative-`GOCACHE` setup failures are retained as setup failures and are not counted as kills.\n+- VALIDATION: `go test ./... -count=1 -v` and `go test ./... -count=1 -cover` passed for all 26 packages; touched-package race tests, `go vet`, native and Windows cross-builds, Windows test compilation/vet, `go mod tidy -diff`, catalog generation check, tracecheck, gofmt, and diff-check passed. Darwin custody runtime is covered; Windows ACL runtime and downstream export/diagnostic consumers remain stated bounds, not invented passes. Exact logs and the write-path census are attached in the rev10 outcome package.\n+- AC: 19 of 21 enumerated production acceptance rows are driven by named production-entry tests and pass. Rows 15 (Windows runtime ACL equivalence) and 21 (consumer/diagnostic export surfaces outside this repository) remain explicit bounds. This is the accepted scope boundary; RPC/TLS/hello/dispatch/stream lifecycle remains with its owning task.\n+- HANDOFF: outcome evidence is ready for independent review. This entry does not claim review acceptance, main integration, or delivery.\n+\n+## 2026-09-16\n+\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev7 — CR6 transaction-family findings repaired at the type level\n+- F1: `migrate` runs inside the authorization transaction (`openLegacyStore` + `WithExclusiveHold` + `revalidateLegacySource` + token-gated `replaceDurably`): legacy writers serialize with joint commits and refuse `ErrMigrationStaleSource` when the source moved. Rev6 unlocked exemption deleted; pre-hold refusals write nothing; opening creates the owner-only skeleton when absent (documented) and fails closed when unopenable. Sync CR6 probe RED pre-fix; post-fix it blocks on the held lock (timeout dump proves the hold, CR5-restore precedent) and the committed async port `TestLegacyMigrateCannotOverwriteCommittedV4` pins serialize-then-refuse-stale + fresh Config4 commit.\n+- F2: `JointCommit` routes replace errors through `resolveFailedReplace` (pin-verified: source-intact aborts with the original error, durable/diverged/unreadable runs compensation restore-or-keep-marker). Both CR6 probes RED pre-fix, green post-fix; marker-kept reopen/forward tests added for apply + rollback (`TestApplyV4FailedReplaceKeepsMarkerWhenRestoreFails` + rollback twin, `TestResolveFailedReplaceKeepsMarker`).\n+- F3/INSTRUMENT: `hosttrust.HeldExclusive` capability (only `exclusiveHold` forges; verified live pre-write; expired on unlock) threaded through all pair writers; `store.lock.exclusive()` signature kept for read paths and probe compat. Static gate rewritten fail-closed (all decls incl. package-var initializers, transitive alias resolution, helper-escape detection, exact (receiver,method) backend pairs, direct-os-mutation rule, hold-entry closures for JointCommit+WithExclusiveHold) with 6 executable rogue controls (4 reviewer verbatim + direct-os.WriteFile + backend-receiver rogue); rev6 token-less plants no longer compile (vet error captured as evidence).\n+- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 33 killed (32 narrowing + 1 call-site) + neutral passed; config 10 killed (9 semantic + 1 label-precision) + neutral passed; new plants hold-require-skip, hold-no-lock, resolve-source-skip, replace-require-skip, legacy-revalidate-skip, replace-restore-skip (each admits exactly one member; kept halves verified in plant logs). Full local validation green: 26/26 packages ok, race ok, cover hosttrust 78.0/config 93.5/peeridentity 97.5/secprim 94.4, 343 top-level PASS 0 FAIL across touched packages, fuzz 13/13, tracecheck/catalog/cigate/JSON/diff-check clean, task-board validate exit 0 with 0 issues for this task. 7 original + 2 F2 exact probes pass on final source. 19/21 AC rows driven, all passing; rows 15/21 retained bounded per CR5/CR6.\n+- LESSON: intermittent \"package X is not in std\"/\"could not import\" battery failures were external go-build-cache interference (different plants each run; serial re-runs kill); batteries re-run with a private GOCACHE. Never run concurrent `go` commands during overlay batteries on this machine.\n+\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev6 — CR5 unlocked-compensation finding repaired as a class\n+- F1: `JointCommit` takes the restore closure and compensates a failed bump under the SAME exclusive hold (`compensateLocked`): marker re-read pin-for-pin, config hash must equal the replacement pin, restore result verified against the source pin before the abort. No reader/writer/boundary can converge between failure and restore. The unlocked `restoreSourceAfterJointFailure` is deleted. Original CR5 probe RED (exit 1, quoted failure) pre-fix; post-fix its in-seam convergence blocks in `flock` (timeout dump proves the hold) and the ported `TestApplyV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit` pins the race as goroutine-vs-gated-restore.\n+- CENSUS: 12-row write-path census (`TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md` board outcome) covers every pair mutation incl. legacy `migrate` (fail-closed row, pinned by `TestLegacyMigrateBesideMarkerRefusesConvergence`), inert credential staging, atomic lock creation, and the sabotage remainder (vanished-marker re-stage). Enforced by committed static gate `TestWritePathCensusGate` + control `TestWritePathGateFlagsUnlockedCaller`; preserve-token order-swap plant `compensate-verify-before-restore` passes the gate and fails only behaviorally.\n+- INTERLEAVINGS: 6 deterministic gated-restore race tests (apply/rollback × reader/writer/held-boundary) + 2 production-entry clean-abort tests + 8 hosttrust compensation tests (tamper/corrupt/unreadable marker, noop+wrong-bytes restore verification, fail-after-write, source-present skip). TEST BUG FOUND BY RACE SUITE ITSELF: boundary tests deadlocked reading trust post-seam on the main goroutine — request now binds pre-seam with a comment.\n+- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 29 narrowing (incl. 4 compensate-*) + 1 call-site + neutral passed; config 6 semantic + 1 label + neutral passed; full local CI replicated green (26 ok, 0 FAIL, 1 pre-existing SKIP; race 26 ok; cover hosttrust 77.9/config 93.3; tracecheck/catalog-6/cigate-contracts-6/claims-6/targets-2/fuzz-13/fixtures 51+59 zero-skip/windows-compile). 7 original reviewer probes re-pass; rows 15/21 retained bounded per CR5.\n+- BOUNDS RESTATED: verifyLockFile 500ms retry rechecks custody without pinning an inode (no external-replacement claim); power-loss beyond fsync unproven; Windows runtime unverified; diagnostics export unowned; spurious-bump corner aborts fail-safe.\n+\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev5 — CR4 surviving-reader + lock-init findings repaired\n+- F1: pending joint-commit marker is now a general admission barrier (`convergeLocked` + shared-to-exclusive dance `lockForConvergedRead`): every read/admission/transaction entry point converges or refuses before exposing a snapshot. Surviving stores converge exactly like reopened ones; stale bindings compare against the recovered generation (never refreshed). Real child-process crash tests (exit 77) cover surviving + reopened × apply + rollback, marker cleanup, and intervened refusal with marker kept.\n+- F2: lock init is atomic non-replacing (O_CREAT|O_EXCL / CREATE_NEW via `FileSystem.CreateExclusive`); losers open the existing inode. Existing-file verify retries 500ms for the create-to-secure window; non-regular refuses immediately. Deterministic cross-process first-open test pins returnedWhileHeld=false + sameInode=true; the replacing-rename mutant restores the exact reviewer failure shape.\n+- F3: native Windows custody tests written (7, build-tagged; vet + test-compile pass, runtime unverified); config backups classified (byte-exact config copies, 0600, excluded names; Windows backup DACLs a stated bound); row-21 handoff persisted with per-surface API/test obligations + notes on all 7 owned tasks, diagnostics explicitly unowned.\n+- MUTANT LESSON: a JointCommit converge-ignore mutant survives because the staged-marker refusal backstops it — error-ignoring mutants are unobservable where a file-level backstop stands. Paired instead: joint-converge-skip (call-site, killed) + recover-forward-no-bump (narrowing, killed) + 8 named convergence tests).\n+- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 25 narrowing + 1 call-site killed + neutral passed; config 4 semantic + 1 label + neutral passed; full local CI replicated green (test/race/cover/tracecheck/catalog/cigate/fuzz-13/fixtures/claims/windows-compile). 19 of 21 AC rows driven; rows 15 (Windows runtime) and 21 (consumers) bounded, n\n[diff truncated]\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree/LOGBOOK.md","added":88,"removed":5},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
