{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dbe7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6d-f2e1-7d43-9e77-843c8eea6221"},"sequence":3150,"recorded_at":1780531400006295,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"9d656e52-9607-486f-955f-021a4f63ae37","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"9d656e52-9607-486f-955f-021a4f63ae37","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"9d656e52-9607-486f-955f-021a4f63ae37"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\n**Outcome:** CR12 candidate for TASK-260909-2ez769 published via handoff (status `to-review`, checklist 22/22). I continued the killed codex run's partial rev12 candidate without discarding any bytes, moved the base to current trunk, re-verified everything on the final tree, and attached real evidence.\n\n**F1 (call-site admission):** census admits interface edges only by exact `*types.Func` object + inventoried source site, with top-level hold-guard dominance for the 4 pair writers; 119 sites enumerated with justifications in the census doc. Committed regression plants renames before AND after `requireHoldForConfig`; narrowing mutant `writepath-interface-callsite-skip` killed by it. Old spelling-based interface admission removed; remaining name-keyed maps are fail-closed concrete detectors (claim narrowed in doc).\n\n**F2 (refused rebind):** `ensureConfigBindingLocked` validates store-side and target-side associations before publishing either. RED-first port of the reviewer's test plus competing-bindings and interrupted-repair pins. My independent RED check fails on unfixed CR11 code with exit 1 and the exact signature; passes post-fix.\n\n**Base:** `refresh-candidate` advanced to trunk `62d4463` (replayed `efe119a`/`5e54874`, signatures verify). Restored stale trunk paths; merged trunk README/LOGBOOK additions preserving both intents (README 55+/0-, LOGBOOK 113+/0- vs new HEAD). Candidate still